\section{Introduction}
\noindent Efficient forecasting is critical for operational planning. Traditional methods often struggle with high-dimensional and non-linear datasets. This document explores a deep learning framework specifically designed for time-series forecasting.

\section{Motivation}
\noindent Demand for real-time insights increased significantly during the pandemic. Traditional models often fail to capture short-term volatility. This work aims to bridge the gap between statistical inference and machine learning.

\section{The Problem}
\noindent Time-series data exhibits non-linear relationships. Features shift with time. Missing values occur frequently. These challenges demand robust algorithms.

\section{Data Preprocessing}
\noindent Data cleaning is essential before modeling.
\begin{itemize}
\item Missing values: Imputation is preferred over deletion.
\item Outlier handling: Remove extreme values.
\item Feature engineering: Transform raw data to capture temporal patterns.
\end{itemize}
\noindent Pipeline:
